# The H713 IOMMU, live — the first kernel that translates VE DMA.
#
#   KERNEL_CONFIG=iommu build/build.sh kernel  ->  build/out/h713-kernel-iommu.fit
#
# Patches 0041 (driver) and 0042 (DTS) put the node at the block's real
# address and attach cedrus as master 0. This fragment turns the driver on;
# the shipping defconfig leaves it off until this has run on hardware.
#
# WHAT TO WATCH FOR ON FIRST BOOT, in order of how bad it is:
#
#   * the board hangs before console output      -> the block was touched
#     ungated, or the address is wrong after all. Recover by loading the
#     production FIT; nothing here is persistent.
#   * "sun50i-iommu ... probe" then nothing      -> good so far.
#   * decode runs and the M1/VA1 ladders stay bit-exact -> the goal.
#   * "Page fault for <addr> (master 0, dir wr)" -> ALSO the goal, in the
#     sense that matters: that line is cedrus writing outside its mappings,
#     which is the bug patch 0040 chases, now reported instead of silently
#     corrupting whatever occupied that memory.
#
# The four drivers are built in for the same reason as builtin-drivers.config:
# a kernel with a different LOCALVERSION has no module tree, so anything that
# must load has to be built in.
CONFIG_SUN50I_IOMMU=y

CONFIG_VIDEO_SUNXI_CEDRUS=y
CONFIG_DRM_SUN50I_H713_AFBD=y
CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST=y
CONFIG_SUNXI_SCANOUT_DMABUF=y

CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ=y
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-iommu"
